## Bonus: giving the model web access with MCP

LM Studio supports MCP servers, so a local model can search the web and fetch pages. I used DuckDuckGo search plus a fetch tool, both run through `uvx`.

`mcp.json` in LM Studio (**replace with your actual config**):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "duckduckgo": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["duckduckgo-mcp-server"]
    },
    "fetch": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["mcp-server-fetch"]
    }
  }
}
```

Keep the tool-call confirmation prompts on. They let you see and approve what the model is doing.

**Future idea:** self-host SearXNG in the homelab and point a SearXNG MCP server at it, so searches go through your own private search engine.

